          %title Basic notions of Categorical algebra
          %h2#BasicNotionsOfCategoricalAlgebra Basic notions of Categorical algebra
          %p
            We have seen that the existence of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+products"} Cartesian products
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            equips is with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo ×
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ×
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathcal{C} \times \mathcal{C}
                  \\overset{ (-) \times (-) }{\longrightarrow}
                  \\mathcal{C}
          %p
            which is directly analogous to the operation of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multiplication"} multiplication
            in an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+algebra"} associative algebra
            or even just in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semigroup"} semigroup
            (or
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vertical+categorification"} categorified
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CartesianMonoidalCategory"}
            below). This is made precise by the concept of a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
            (Def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MonoidalCategory"}
            below).
          %p
            This relation between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra"} algebra
            leads to the fields of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+algebra"} categorical algebra
            and of
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+algebra"} universal algebra
          %p
            Here we are mainly interested in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+categories"} monoidal categories
            as a foundations for
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category+theory"} enriched category theory
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#EnrichedCategories"} below
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %h3#monoidal_categories Monoidal categories
          #MonoidalCategory.num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"}> monoidal category
                )
            %p
              An_
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"}> monoidal category
              _ is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              (Def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Categories"}
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
                  (Def.
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Functors"}
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mo ×
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi 𝒞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\otimes
                        \\;\colon\;
                        \\mathcal{C} \times \mathcal{C}
                        \\longrightarrow
                        \\mathcal{C}
                %p
                  out of the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+category"} product category
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                  with itself (Example
                  = succeed ")," do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ProductCategory"}
                  = succeed "," do
                    %strong
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
              %li
                %p
                  an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi Obj
                          %mi 𝒞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        1 \in Obj_{\mathcal{C}}
                %p
                  called the
                  %strong
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+object"} unit object
                  or
                  = succeed "," do
                    %strong
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+unit"} tensor unit
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural isomorphism
                  (Def.
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#NaturalTransformations"}
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mover
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mo ≃
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        a
                        \\;\colon\;
                        ((-)\otimes (-)) \otimes (-)
                        \\overset{\simeq}{\longrightarrow}
                        (-) \otimes ((-)\otimes(-))
                %p
                  called the
                  = succeed "," do
                    %strong
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associator"} associator
              %li#MonoidalCategoryUnitors
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural isomorphism
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℓ
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mover
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mo ≃
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\ell
                        \\;\colon\;
                        (1 \otimes (-))
                        \\overset{\simeq}{\longrightarrow}
                        (-)
                %p
                  called the
                  = succeed "," do
                    %strong
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+unitor"} left unitor
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi r
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
